1) Neutral wizard that starts with Charm Monster, finds speed boots
and magic whistle (also a second copy of Charm Monster) in a store on
DLVL3.  Sokoban has a bag of holding (which was useful, since I had no
bag to that point).  Co-aligned priest in minetown, so no issues with
alignment.  Reaches the Medusa level at CLVL5, which is the Titan
version.  Decides to wait for the Titan to be adjacent and using
Elbereth, take 3 chances at Charm Monster on it.  Titan has a wand of
fire.  I don't realize this until after he has hit me once, and the
second hit is enough to kill me.  DYWYPI?

2) Knight.  Finds a wand of wishing in a store on DLVL2.  Silver DSM,
figurine of an archon, magic whistle.  Lose pacifism to an unknown
boulder trap in the mines (and kill a few other monsters after a trap
door), but still have weaponless conduct, and playing "mostly
pacifist".  Find a cloak of MR and helm of brilliance in a bones pile,
alchemize 16 potions of full healing, so I am at 150HP with all
resistances, base AC of -1, WIS of 22.  The titan on Medusa is
peaceful, but I skip the level by jumping downward.  Castle and Valley
of the Dead are cleared.  As I was nearly strained with junk in my
blessed bag of holding, I wish up a spellbook of identify (35% fail or
so with a robe on) and ID a bunch of stuff.  As I climb back up to my
stash, an Umber Hulk confuses my pet archon.  The archon hits!  The
archon hits!  Oh no, he's using the touch of death!  DYWYPI?  I forgot
to switch back from the robe to the CoMR.

3) Neutral caveman.  Don't find entrance to the mines.  Two armor
stores on DLVL2 and 4, get Gauntlets of Power and cloaks of
invisibility, displacement, and protection.  On level 5 (Oracle
level), discover a wand.  Still pacifist, atheist, illiterate.
Engrave with it.  Wishing.  Wish up a scroll of charging, figuring
I'll wait a bit longer to figure out if I want an Archon again or
not.  Immediately fall into a pit and have 3HP left, and a giant rat
kills me before I could wish anything up to save myself.


